  "goodToKnow": "Die Abschiebung is deportation: Ihm droht die Abschiebung. It applies to people without a right to stay, such as rejected asylum seekers. If deportation can't happen, for example because of illness or missing papers, they may get a Duldung (temporary suspension). Abschiebungen are a constant topic in German migration debates. The verb abschieben also means, casually, to shove off or offload: Verantwortung abschieben (to pass the buck)."
